        "original_id": "af08c4d7-059b-5a1e-b9c5-a57c7c2a0bd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Chvrches, Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie\n- People: Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, Martin Doherty, Martin Metcalfe, John Duncan, Fin Wilson, Shirley Manson, Rona Scobie, Derek Kelly\n- Songs and Albums: \"Make Them Gold\", Every Open Eye\n- Places: Bathgate, Edinburgh, Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie was a Scottish rock group from the 1980s and 1990s that formed in Bathgate near Edinburgh, Scotland.\n- Shirley Manson was a backing vocalist and keyboard player for Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie from 1981 to 1992.\n- At Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie's commercial peak, the band's line-up included Martin Metcalfe on vocals, John Duncan on guitar, Fin Wilson on bass guitar, Shirley Manson and Rona Scobie on keyboards and backing vocals, and Derek Kelly on drums.\n- Chvrches consists of Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, and Martin Doherty.\n- In Chvrches, Lauren Mayberry performs lead vocals, drums, additional synthesisers, and samplers.\n- In Chvrches, Iain Cook performs synthesisers, guitar, bass, and vocals.\n- In Chvrches, Martin Doherty performs synthesisers, samplers, and vocals.\n- \"Make Them Gold\" is a song by the Scottish synthpop band Chvrches from the band's second studio album Every Open Eye.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c37017ef-a3c2-57d6-99cb-0d4b765563d6",
